   "name": "The Flat Rate Movers \u2014 Piano, Antique and White-Glove Operations Dataset",
   "description": "Piano, antique and white-glove operations from The Flat Rate Movers. Company scope (published): white-glove handling of pianos, antiques and high-value items \u2014 surveyed, protected, and moved with custom crating when the piece requires it, at one flat rate agreed in writing. The work runs piece by piece, never bulk: each piece is assessed on its own \u2014 weight, fragile points, finish and value at risk \u2014 then wrapped, padded or crated to match; furniture and pieces travel fully covered in padded blankets and sealed with clear stretch wrap, and pieces that need more get a custom crate built around them. The audiences are published: collectors, estates and high-value households; museums, collectors, galleries and estates moving pieces that cannot be replaced; and \u2014 on the Martinsburg branch page \u2014 high-value, sensitive-asset owners, including medical and museum clients. Scheduling is discreet by design: high-value work is scheduled quietly, handled without spectacle, and no client is named, ever. Heavy pieces join the same plan: pianos, safes and other high-mass pieces of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs are planned under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol inside the same job \u2014 route surveyed, floor checked to L/360, placement verified. Export pieces are packed and crated to ISPM 15 when the journey crosses a border.",
