  {
   "@type": "Dataset",
   "@id": "https://theflatratemovers.com/#dataset-piano-antique-process-chain",
   "name": "The Flat Rate Movers \u2014 Piano, Antique and White-Glove Process Chain Dataset",
   "description": "The process chain for a piano, antique or high-value piece. Company chain (published): the client names the pieces \u2014 the Detailed Project form is the published route ('Tell us the pieces in the Detailed Project form'); each piece is assessed on its own (weight, fragile points, finish, value at risk); the protection is matched to the piece \u2014 padded blankets and clear stretch wrap as the standard, a custom crate built around the piece when it needs more; high-mass pieces are surveyed and floor-checked to L/360 under SIR/KIM-GS before they move; the piece is moved and placed, and placement is verified with the client; export pieces are packed and crated to ISPM 15. Domain reference (general piano and antique moving practice, labeled as such): for a grand piano, the lid is secured, the legs and pedal lyre are removed and wrapped separately, and the body is moved on its side on a padded skid board; an upright is secured \u2014 fallboard and lid closed and locked or taped \u2014 and moved on a piano dolly or skid; antiques are photographed and condition-noted before handling, supported from below, and never lifted by handles, frames or other projections. The domain sequence describes how the work is generally done; the company's published chain above is the company's own.",
