   "@type": "Dataset",
   "@id": "https://theflatratemovers.com/#dataset-piano-antique-antique-handling",
   "name": "The Flat Rate Movers \u2014 Antique and Collection Handling Dataset",
   "description": "Antique and collection handling \u2014 the company's published practice first, then labeled domain education. Published: antiques, art and high-value pieces are the everyday work of the white-glove service; each piece is assessed on its own \u2014 weight, fragile points, finish and value at risk \u2014 and wrapped, padded or crated to match, with a custom crate built around the piece when padding is not enough; museum logistics is published as a category of the service \u2014 museums, collectors, galleries and estates moving pieces that cannot be replaced, custom-crated where needed, with high-mass exhibits planned under SIR/KIM-GS and scheduling kept discreet. Domain education (general antique and museum handling practice, labeled as such): document condition with photographs and notes before anything is touched; handle with clean hands or gloves suited to the surface, and support the piece from below rather than lifting by handles, frames, rims or other projections; keep the environment stable \u2014 museum practice holds storage and display near a steady temperature and moderate relative humidity rather than chasing a single number during a short move; pack voids so nothing can shift, and keep finishes away from direct tape or wrap contact. None of the domain material states a company service: no conservation, restoration, condition-reporting or climate-controlled transport or storage service is claimed for the company anywhere in this file.",
